      "body": "## Purpose\r\n\r\nReduce the runtime of the sequence-parallel correctness suite by pruning a redundant test dimension.\r\n\r\nThe last successful run took approximately 73.5 minutes. The 32-case tiny-Llama matrix accounted for roughly 63 minutes, while the prompt-embedding cases took about 10 minutes.\r\n\r\n`SPTestSettings.fast()` previously crossed `chunked_prefill=False` and `True`. However, `False` only omitted the CLI flag; automatic configuration still enabled chunked prefill for this model. Both cases therefore exercised the same\r\neffective configuration.\r\n\r\nThis change tests chunked prefill explicitly once while retaining:\r\n\r\n- Pipeline parallelism with PP=1 and PP=2.\r\n- CUDAGraph enabled and disabled.\r\n- MP and Ray distributed backends.\r\n- Inductor graph partitioning enabled and disabled.\r\n\r\nThe tiny-Llama matrix is reduced from 32 to 16 cases, and the complete suite from 45 to 29 cases, without adding GPU concurrency. FP8, prompt-embedding, NVFP4, and `SPTestSettings.detailed()` coverage remain unchanged.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest --collect-only -q \\\r\n  tests/compile/correctness_e2e/test_sequence_parallel.py\r\n\r\n.venv/bin/pre-commit run --files \\\r\n  tests/compile/correctness_e2e/test_sequence_parallel.py\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Test Results\r\n\r\n```bash\r\nTotal collection: 29 tests, reduced from 45.\r\nTiny-Llama: 16 tests, reduced from 32.\r\nFP8: 8 tests.\r\nPrompt embeddings: 4 tests.\r\nNVFP4: 1 test.\r\n```",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "mgoin"
            },
            "body": "Could we simply prune the number/length of testing down? I'd like to investigate the test time breakdown",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-04T17:43:11Z",
            "databaseId": 5182598320,
            "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T17:43:11Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/51048#issuecomment-5182598320"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "taneem-ibrahim"
            },
            "body": "> Could we simply prune the number/length of testing down? I'd like to investigate the test time breakdown\r\n\r\nYes, that's an option too if we don't want to add another GPU worker. Currently we have this set up for SPTestSettings.fast() test combinations :\r\n\r\n```\r\nCUDAGraph mode: on/off\r\nPipeline parallelism: PP=1/2\r\nChunked-prefill flag: False/True\r\n\r\n```\r\nThis combined with MP/Ray and graph partitioning on/off permutations and combinations, we have tiny-Llama running 32 test cases.\r\n\r\nI updated the PR to set `chunked_prefill=True` since vLLM will enable it automatically anyway, so that trims off all the possible combinations with `chunked_prefill=False`. We end up with the following prunings as a result:\r\n\r\n```\r\nTiny-Llama: 32 → 16 cases\r\nComplete suite: 45 → 29 cases\r\n```",
            "createdAt": "2026-08-04T22:10:31Z",
            "databaseId": 5185187073,
            "updatedAt": "2026-08-04T22:11:14Z",
